  "notes": [
    "Every font file is an unmodified upstream file from the google/fonts repository at the pinned commit. Nothing is subset, renamed or re-encoded.",
    "Each OFL.txt is the upstream licence text with its line endings converted from CRLF to LF; the wording is unchanged.",
    "Only upright faces ship. The engine never draws italic or slanted text, so the italic files of Rubik, IBM Plex Sans and Inter are left out.",
    "wght is an inclusive [min, max] range on every file: a variable font spans its weight axis, a static font repeats its single weight. weights lists the 100-step stops that fall inside the family range.",
    "scripts lists what a family is meant to typeset in a design; latin is the Latin coverage measured in coverage.json (extended: accented letters of Latin-1, basic: printable ASCII, none). Offer a family for a role by scripts and roles; use latin to know whether Latin runs, digits and handles can stay in the same face.",
    "axes[].use: free means the engine sets the axis per token; auto means it is left to font-optical-sizing; default-only means the engine never sets it, so the font default applies (Cairo's slnt stays 0 and no slant is drawn).",
    "tashkeel: ok means the font maps U+064B-0652 and positions marks (GPOS mark and mkmk for Arabic); limited means marks are mapped but not positioned; none means no support.",
    "An export that embeds a family as a base64 @font-face must carry that family's copyright line and licence text: copyright, reservedFontNames and licenseFile are recorded for that purpose.",
    "Maintained with tools/font_coverage.py, which rewrites coverage.json from the cmap and, with --check, verifies bytes, sha256, weights and axes here against the files."
  ],
